# Bernoulli(3/2) is not a distribution: the program has no meaning.
# Expected: refused with one line naming the probability.  The choice rule
# 3/2 * wp(x := 1, f) - 1/2 * wp(x := 0, f) used to be applied as it stands, giving the
# expectation of x as 3/2, above the largest value x can take.
x ~ Bernoulli(3/2);
return x
?Ex[x] >= 1.5
